<p>The <strong>under desk elliptical vs treadmill</strong> choice is really a choice between two ways of working. A seated under desk elliptical lets you keep your chair and desk and pedal quietly while you type. An under desk treadmill, often sold as a walking pad, gets you on your feet and walking at a slow pace beside or under a standing desk.</p>
<p>The treadmill wins on calorie burn and step counts. The elliptical wins on price, noise, comfort and how easily it fits into a normal workday. If you sit at a fixed-height desk, the decision is already made for you: get the elliptical. If you own a standing desk, read on, because it is a closer call.</p>

<h2>Under Desk Elliptical vs Treadmill: Side by Side</h2>
<div class="table-wrap"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Factor</th><th>Under desk elliptical</th><th>Under desk treadmill</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>How you use it</td><td>Seated, pedaling</td><td>Standing, walking (some models also jog)</td></tr>
